Well, from time to time people complain about unfair deaths, and how
frustrating they are.  I'd agree with the latest complainer, that the
game would be no worse, and a perhaps better, without instant death
traps.

However, FAR more frustrating is the fact that most of the deaths that
I suffer are STUPID ones!  80-90% of the time, I die and then realise
that I needn't have...

This time: my best character for quite some games (I'm a relative
beginner) AC -4 (my best ever) gets surrounded by hill orcs after
dealing with a mumak near the bottom of the mines.  quaffs a healing
potion, but is still carking.  Zaps a wand of sleep - Nothing Happens.
Dies.  Possessions: wand of teleport(1).

Grrrr  ... I forgot to name it when I worked out what it was!  Then I
overlooked it!!  So many mistakes!  So often!  This is what makes the
game so frustrating - and addicting!  The knowledge that _next_ time
you'll _really_ be careful...

Martin.





